# Web Angular Tailwind

## Modern Angular Patterns (v21+)

- **Use standalone components** – `standalone: true` in component decorator
- **Use Signals for state** – Prefer `signal()` and `computed()` over RxJS where appropriate
- **Use modern template syntax** – `@if`, `@for`, `@switch` instead of structural directives
- **Use typed reactive forms** – `FormControl<string>`, `FormGroup<MyForm>`

## CSS-First Tailwind 4.x

- **Use CSS-first configuration** – Define design tokens with `@theme` in CSS
- **Use component classes** for controls (buttons, inputs, cards)
- **Use utilities** for layout and spacing
- **Use `class`** (not `className`) in Angular templates

## E2E Testing Requirements

**MUST add `data-testid` to:**
- All interactive elements (buttons, links, inputs, selects)
- Form containers and validation message containers
- Key containers (cards, modals, sidebars)
- Dynamic content areas (lists, tables)
- Navigation elements

```html
<!-- ✅ CORRECT: data-testid for testing -->
<button data-testid="submit-button" class="btn-primary" (click)="onSubmit()">
  Submit
</button>

<input
  data-testid="email-input"
  type="email"
  formControlName="email"
  class="input"
/>

<div data-testid="user-card" class="card">
  <!-- card content -->
</div>
```

## Angular CLI via MCP

**ALWAYS prefer Angular CLI MCP tools** for Angular workflows:
- Generating components, services, modules
- Running builds, tests, and dev server
- Managing dependencies

## Template Syntax

```html
<!-- ✅ CORRECT: Modern syntax -->
@if (user) {
  <div>{{ user.name }}</div>
}

@for (item of items; track item.id) {
  <div>{{ item.name }}</div>
}

@switch (status) {
  @case ('active') {
    <span>Active</span>
  }
  @case ('inactive') {
    <span>Inactive</span>
  }
  @default {
    <span>Unknown</span>
  }
}

<!-- ❌ WRONG: Old structural directives -->
<div *ngIf="user">{{ user.name }}</div>
<div *ngFor="let item of items">{{ item.name }}</div>
```

## Reactive Forms

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT: Typed reactive forms
interface LoginForm {
  email: FormControl<string>;
  password: FormControl<string>;
}

form = this.fb.group<LoginForm>({
  email: this.fb.control('', { validators: [Validators.required, Validators.email], nonNullable: true }),
  password: this.fb.control('', { validators: [Validators.required], nonNullable: true }),
});
```
